# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the re-record of the packed-any evidence on the K64j-OQ binary (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/oneq-ship and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. ONE TAG AT A TIME; wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job.
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. A placeholder in @...@ is filled in by whoever drives the window (@SERVED_IMAGE@: the served
# image's reference; @K64J_OQ_GRAFT_DIR@ and @K64J_OQ_TTNNCPP_SHA256@: the K64j-OQ graft directory and its binary's digest, the K64J_OQ_TTNNCPP_SHA256 line of OQ-L1 and
# packed_any_admission.K64J_OQ_TTNNCPP_SHA256). C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the window's image (the image OQ-B0 built, tp4-oneq-1: sed -i 's/tp4-fusion-1/<tag>/' *.env): an EVIDENCE job runs this checkout's harness in it.
# An EVIDENCE job: one harness on card M alone (C2_CARDS=pair: cardm is a pair-shaped step; only RQ0 resets the four boards). The K64j-OQ binary is pinned by EXPECT_TTNNCPP_SHA256 and mounted
# over the image's: read the launched argv, a graft mounted is not a graft executed. The harness is the K64j one (optimisation/ttnn-op/k64j): K64j-OQ carries K64j's four decode kernels and
# the chain reader byte for byte (the K64j-OQ build proves it), so the same sections, seeds and extents re-run on the new binary. A watcher job (W) runs before its full job and is not
# evidence; a REDUCED-PASS or a reduced scope is never evidence. After the last job of a window: scripts/ci/record_packed_any_evidence_tp4.py --binary k64j-oq (README of
# optimisation/ttnn-op/sdpa_prefill_oneq, 'Landing the K64j-OQ records').
# RQ0 (STOP): reset all four boards (card M alone does not open after four-card jobs: v140). Once per window, first. Duration (estimate): 12 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-fusion-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-gate
